    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** serves as our primary anchor with a score of 56.89. Despite a challenging matchup against Smith, H (L) who sports a 3.07 xERA, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a must-start due to his elevated batting order position and high base projection. **Jonathan Aranda** follows with a 52.17 score; while facing a pitcher of Cole's caliber is never ideal, the platoon advantage against the right-hander provides a significant lift that keeps him firmly in our starting 1B slot. **Will Smith** rounds out the active trio at 46.29; his performance is tempered by the matchup against Dodd (L), but his prime spot in the #3 hole and solid xwOBA ensure he remains above the benching threshold.\n\nThe most difficult decision of the day involved **Braden Montgomery**, who narrowly missed the starting lineup with a 36.98 score. While his switch-hitting ability provided a +3% boost, the combination of a daunting matchup against Messick (L) and a low-leverage #8 spot in the order pushed him below our 40.0 floor. We are opting to bench him to preserve game caps, prioritizing the efficiency of our core trio over his marginal upside. With **Bryce Harper**, **Lawrence Butler**, and **Justin Crawford** sidelined due to team off-days, our bench depth is significantly constrained. We will continue to monitor the status of **Cal Raleigh**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Matt Chapman**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Zack Gelof**, **Luis Arraez**, **Masyn Winn**, **Brendan Donovan**, **JJ Bleday**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Alex Freeland** for any late-breaking lineup changes, as the risk of \"Lineup Pending\" designations remains a primary concern for the lower end of our roster today.",
